<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmad al-Mustain II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1110</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as al-Musta'in II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmad al-Mustain II (died 1110) was the Hudid king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">Taifa</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a> from 1085, the last of his line to rule the city. He paid tribute to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>, lost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huesca">Huesca</a> to Aragon after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-alcoraz">Battle of Alcoraz</a> in 1096, and faced growing Aragonese pressure. He was killed fighting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-i-of-aragon">Alfonso I of Aragon</a> at Valtierra in January 1110, after which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a> occupied Zaragoza.</p></div>
